  _menuDescription: DOES NOT like bannas, DO NOT FEED BANANNAS
  _funFacts:
  - _fact: "Capuchin monkeys are some of the only primates, other than apes, known
      to use tools\u2014like rocks\u2014to crack open nuts in the wild."
  - _fact: The howler monkey has an amazing call that can carry up to 3 miles through
      dense rainforests.
  - _fact: Japanese macaques, also known as snow monkeys, have evolved to thrive
      in climates ranging from subtropical to subarctic.  Troops of snow monkeys
      frequent the volcanic hot springs (onsens) at Jigokudani Monkey Park in Yamanouchi,
      Japan.
  - _fact: The patas monkey can reach running speeds of up to 35 mph, making it the
      fastest of all primates.
